      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The state of microcirculation was studied in 35 patients with obliterating atherosclerosis of the lower extremity vessels (1st group) and 36 patients with extensive atherosclerosis having a combined impairment of the peripheral basin: arteries of lower extremities and coronary arteries (2nd group) treated using the method of plasmapheresis (PPh) and PPh combined with intravascular laser irradiation of blood (IVLIB). The isolated use of PPh in patients of the 1st group was established to be effective, while combination of PPh and IVLIB was necessary for the patients of the 2nd group."},
